  "actionResultText": "Here's your interactive graph plotting both functions! Here's what to explore:\n\n- **$y = x^2$** — a upward-opening parabola with its vertex at the origin $(0, 0)$.\n- **$y = 2x + 1$** — a straight line with slope $2$ and y-intercept $1$.\n\n### 🔍 Key Feature: Intersection Points\nThe two curves meet where $x^2 = 2x + 1$. Solving:\n\n$$x^2 - 2x - 1 = 0 \\implies x = 1 \\pm \\sqrt{2}$$\n\nSo the intersection points are approximately $(-0.414,\\ 0.172)$ and $(2.414,\\ 5.828)$.\n\n### How to use the Spark:\n- **Hover** over the curves to see coordinates at any point.\n- **Click** on an expression to edit it — try changing the slope or the exponent!\n- **Zoom/pan** with your mouse or trackpad to explore different regions.",
